#%PAM-1.0
#
# Unlocking the screen with a fingerprint. wlrix-lock runs this stack beside `wlrix-lock`, on a
# thread of its own, so the finger and the password are both accepted at once and whichever
# succeeds first unlocks -- KDE's arrangement, not the one-after-the-other a single stack gives.
#
# pam_fprintd alone: no password module, so this stack never asks for one. `default=die` hands
# back pam_fprintd's own answer rather than pam_deny's -- a timeout, too many mismatches, no
# reader -- which is what wlrix-lock decides when to try again by. The leading `-` skips the line
# if fprintd is not installed, which leaves pam_deny: only the password unlocks.

-auth      [success=done default=die]  pam_fprintd.so
auth       required     pam_deny.so
account    include      system-auth
